# Her day (one topic a day). Her line answers "how's your day", from her mood, what happened to her today and her voice.
# Slots: name you laugh pet voice tone mood moodword thing period place club exam rel; {who} when something happened with another girl.

# ---------------- you ask ----------------
@rule me.day.plain
on me.day
- [How's your day going|How's today treating you|How has your day been], {name}?
- [So|Hey], how's [the day|everything] going?
- You doing okay today?

@rule me.day.who
on me.day
when verb=ate_with kind=day
- How was lunch with {who}?
- [Did you|So you] have lunch with {who}? How was it?
- [I saw you eating with {who}.|You and {who} at lunch, huh?] What did you two talk about?

@rule me.day.fight
on me.day
when verb=fought|insulted kind=day
- I heard something happened with {who}. You okay?
- Is everything alright between you and {who}?
- [People are saying you and {who} argued.|I heard you and {who} fell out.] Want to talk about it?

@rule me.day.madeup
on me.day
when verb=made_up kind=day
- So you and {who} are good again?
- [I saw you and {who} talking again.|Heard you patched things up with {who}.] Glad?
- [You and {who} made up, right?|Peace with {who} at last?] That's good to hear.

@rule me.day.dating
on me.day
when verb=started_dating kind=day
- So... you and {who}, huh?
- [Word is you're going out with {who} now.|You and {who}? Since when?]
- [So it's true about you and {who}?|Congratulations, I think? You and {who}.]

@rule me.day.close
on me.day
when rel=girlfriend|lover
- Hey, you. How's [my favorite person|your day] [doing|going]?
- [There you are.|Hey.] How's your day been?
- [Hi, beautiful.|Hey, you.] [Did you miss me today?|Tell me about your day.]

# ---------------- her answer, by mood ----------------
@rule day.fine
on day
when mood=none
opens ask,share,tease
- [It's been pretty normal.|Nothing special, really.|Same as always.] [Classes, friends, the usual.|Just a regular day.]
- [Normal, I guess.|Pretty okay.] [Nothing's happened yet.|Nothing worth telling... yet.]
- [Hm, it's fine.|Not bad.] [How about yours?|What about you?]

@rule day.cheerful
on day
when mood=cheerful
opens ask,tease,share
feel smile
- [Really good, actually!|Great!|It's been a good one!] [Everything's going my way today.|I don't even know why, I'm just in a good mood.|Even the teachers were nice today.]
- [I'm in such a good mood today.|Today's one of those days where everything clicks.] [Can you tell?|It shows, huh?]
- [It's been lovely.|Honestly? Great.] [I hope it stays like this.|I could get used to days like this.]

@rule day.hungry
on day
when mood=hungry
opens invite,tease,share
- [Honestly? I'm starving.|I'm so hungry I can't think.|My stomach has been growling all class.] [I skipped breakfast.|Lunch can't come soon enough.|I'd kill for some bread right now.]
- [Ugh, all I can think about is food.|Is it lunch yet? Please say yes.]
- [Food. I need food.|My stomach is louder than the teacher.] [Do you have anything?|Is the cafeteria still open?]

@rule day.hungry.lunch
on day
when mood=hungry period=lunch
opens invite,tease
- [Perfect timing, I'm starving.|Finally, lunch.] [I could eat a whole bento by myself. Two, maybe.|I've been waiting for this all morning.]
- [Lunchtime at last!|Don't get between me and lunch.] [I'm not sharing. Okay, maybe a little.|I'm running to the store.]
- [Lunch!|Thank god, lunch.] [I'm going to eat so much.|Want to eat together?]

@rule day.bored
on day
when mood=bored
opens invite,tease,ask
- [Boring.|So boring.|Slow. So slow.] [Nothing's happening.|Every class felt three hours long.|I've been staring at the clock all day.]
- [I'm bored out of my mind.|Today is dragging.] [Entertain me?|Got anything fun?|Save me, please.]
- [Today's been dull.|Nothing interesting ever happens.] [Do something crazy.|Even the clouds are boring.]

@rule day.stressed
on day
when mood=stressed
opens comfort,ask,invite
feel worried
- [Kind of rough.|Not great, honestly.|Stressful.] [I can't stop worrying about {mything}.|I've got so much to do.|I feel like I'm falling behind.]
- [Honestly? I'm a bit overwhelmed.|Don't ask...] [It's {mything}. It's all too much right now.|There's too much going on.]
- [Stressed, honestly.|Too much, too fast.] [My to-do list keeps growing.|I can't catch a break.]

@rule day.stressed.exam
on day
when mood=stressed exam=yes
opens comfort,invite,ask
feel worried
- [The exams.|It's the exams.] [I studied all night and I still feel like I know nothing.|My head is full of formulas.|If I fail, my parents will...]
- [Exam week is killing me.|I can't stop thinking about the exams.] [How are you so calm?|Are you ready?]
- [Exams are breathing down my neck.|I keep blanking on everything.] [Quiz me?|I'm doomed.]

@rule day.lonely
on day
when mood=lonely
opens comfort,invite,ask
feel sad
- [Kind of lonely, actually.|Quiet. Too quiet.|Eh... a bit lonely.] [My friends were all busy today.|I ate by myself.|Nobody's really been around.]
- [It's been a long day by myself.|I haven't really talked to anyone today.] [...Until now, I guess.|So, thanks for stopping.]
- [Kind of empty, today.|Lonely, if I'm honest.] [Everyone had somewhere to be.|It's nice that you came.]

@rule day.flirty
on day
when mood=flirty
opens tease,praise,invite
feel smile
- [Better now that you're here.|Mm, it just got better.|Pretty good... and getting better.]
- [I've been in a strange mood all day.|I don't know, I feel kind of... restless today.] [Is that weird?|Don't look at me like that.]
- [Good. Very good.|My day? Mm, interesting.] [Thinking about someone.|Getting more interesting.]

@rule day.sleepy
on day
when mood=sleepy
opens tease,comfort,ask
- [Sleepy...|So sleepy.|Mmh... tired.] [I stayed up way too late last night.|I almost fell asleep in class.|The teacher caught me nodding off.]
- [*yawn* Sorry.|Don't mind me, I'm half asleep.] [Last night was a mistake.|I need a nap. Badly.]
- [My eyes keep closing.|Is it bedtime yet?] [Talk slowly.|I'm running on empty.]

@rule day.upset
on day
when mood=upset
opens comfort,ask
feel pout
- [Don't ask.|Bad.|Honestly? Awful.] [I don't want to talk about it.|Everything's going wrong.|Just one of those days.]
- [I'm... not in a good mood today.|Today can just end already.] [Sorry. It's not you.|Just... don't take it personally.]
- [Terrible, okay?|Not good.] [Can we not?|I'd rather not get into it.]

# ---------------- something that happened to her today ----------------
@rule day.lunch.with
on day
when realverb=ate_with kind=day how=participant
opens ask,tease,share
feel smile
- [It was nice!|Lunch with {who} was fun.] [We talked the whole time.|{Who} shared her side dish with me.|We ended up laughing about something stupid.]
- [Oh, you saw?|Yeah, we ate together.] [{Who}'s easy to talk to.|I like eating with {who}.]
- [Lunch was the best part of the day.|{Who} and I ate on the roof.] [{Who} is so funny.|The view was great.]

@rule day.fight.with
on day
when realverb=fought|insulted kind=day how=participant
opens comfort,ask,defend
feel sad
- [...You heard about that?|It was nothing.|We had words.] [{Who} said something and I snapped.|I don't even know how it started.|I'm still mad, honestly.]
- [Don't get me started on {who}.|Me and {who}... it's complicated right now.]
- [{Who} and I aren't talking.|Ugh, {who}.] [She knows what she did.|I don't want to talk about it.]

@rule day.madeup.with
on day
when realverb=made_up kind=day how=participant
opens praise,ask,share
feel smile
- [Yeah, we're okay now.|We talked it out.] [I'm glad, honestly. I missed {who}.|It was stupid of us to fight.]
- [{Who} and I made up.|We're fine now, {who} and me.] [I said sorry first.|It feels good.]
- [Yeah, me and {who} are back to normal.|It's over. We're friends again.] [What a relief.|We laughed about it after.]

@rule day.dating.with
on day
when realverb=started_dating kind=day how=participant
opens tease,ask,praise
feel shy
- [Ah... so people are talking already?|Y-yeah. Me and {who}.] [It just sort of happened.|Don't make a big deal out of it.|I'm still not used to saying it.]
- [Um... yes. {Who} and I are going out.|So, it's official. Me and {who}.] [I'm still pinching myself.|Please don't tease me.]
- [You found out about {who}?|Hehe... yeah.] [It's real.|Be happy for me?]

# ---------------- voices: the same moods, the way some girls say them ----------------
@rule day.cheerful.genki
on day
when mood=cheerful voice=genki|energetic
opens ask,tease,invite
feel laugh
- [AMAZING!|The best!|Super good!] [I ran all the way here!|I got a perfect score on the quiz!|I feel like I could do anything today!]
- [GREAT!|Awesome!] [Today's my lucky day!|Everything's going my way!]
- [Fantastic!|Couldn't be better!] [I won at rock-paper-scissors five times!|The sun's out and I'm full of energy!]

@rule day.fine.cool
on day
when mood=none voice=cool|serious|proper
opens ask,share
- [Uneventful.|Productive enough.|Nothing to report.] [Classes went as planned.|I finished my assignments.]
- [It's a day.|It's fine.] [Why do you ask?|Is there a reason you want to know?]
- [Ordinary.|Fine.] [Nothing worth mentioning.|I have no complaints.]

@rule day.fine.tsundere
on day
when mood=none voice=tsundere
opens tease,ask
feel pout
- [W-why do you care?|What's it to you?] [It was fine. Totally fine.|...It was okay, if you must know.]
- [Not that it matters to you, but fine.|My day? Hmph.] [Don't think I was waiting for you.|It was... fine.]
- [Stop asking like you care.|It was average, okay?] [...Thanks for asking, I guess.|Whatever.]

@rule day.fine.gyaru
on day
when mood=none voice=gyaru|open
opens tease,share,invite
- [Ugh, so-so.|Meh.|Kinda chill.] [Class was dead, but whatever.|I spent half of it doing my nails under the desk.|Nothing cute happened yet.]
- [Same old, same old.|Eh, chill.] [Need something fun to happen.|Whatcha got for me?]
- [Lowkey boring, ngl.|Mid, honestly.] [Teacher confiscated my phone.|Spice it up for me?]

@rule day.fine.shy
on day
when mood=none voice=shy|bookish
opens ask,share
feel shy
- [Ah... it's been okay.|N-nothing special.] [I read during break.|I just... sat in my seat, mostly.]
- [It was quiet.|U-um, it was fine.] [Like usual.|Thank you for asking.]
- [Nothing happened, really.|Okay, I think.] [I like quiet days.|Is that boring?]

@rule day.sleepy.lazy
on day
when mood=sleepy voice=lazy|airhead
opens tease,invite
- [Mmh... what day is it?|Was I asleep just now?] [School should start at noon.|I dreamed about pudding.]
- [Zzz... huh? Oh, hi.|Five more minutes...] [I wasn't sleeping.|Sleep is the best class.]
- [Tired. So tired.|Mmmh.] [My bed is calling me.|Carry me home?]

@rule day.lonely.close
on day
when mood=lonely rel=girlfriend|lover
opens comfort,invite
feel sad
- [I missed you today.|Where were you all morning?] [I kept looking for you between classes.|It's lonely when you're not around.]
- [I kept thinking of you all day.|It's better now that you're here.] [Stay with me a bit?|Don't leave yet.]
- [I waited for you at the gate.|The day felt so long without you.] [Silly, right?|Hug?]

@rule day.stressed.club
on day
when mood=stressed period=after|club
opens comfort,ask,invite
feel worried
- [The {club} is a mess right now.|Club stuff.] [Everyone's counting on me.|We're behind on everything.]
- [The {club} is driving me crazy.|We've got a deadline at the {club}.] [I need a break.|Tell me something nice.]
- [I'm exhausted from the {club}.|Club drama again.] [I just want to sleep.|Don't ask.]


# Her day, where the place and the weather change what she says (the rain, the library, a fight on her mind).

@rule day.rain.library.books.fight
on day
when kind=day placeid=library l_study=yes wet=yes fight=yes
opens comfort,ask
feel shy
- [I came to the library to read with the rain on the windows.|Rain, a book, and a quiet corner. That's my day.|I've been reading here since lunch, listening to the rain.] [It helps me forget about {fightwho}. A little.|I needed it, after the fight with {fightwho}.|Better than thinking about {fightwho}.]
- [Honestly? The rain is the best part of today.|My day's been... quiet. On purpose.] [{Fightwho} and I had a fight, so I hid in here with a book.|After {fightwho}, I just wanted rain and pages.]
- [It's the kind of day you read through.|I'm on my second book already.] [The rain helps. So does not seeing {fightwho}.|Don't ask about {fightwho}. Ask about the book.]

@rule day.rain.library.books
on day
when kind=day placeid=library l_study=yes wet=yes
opens share,invite
feel smile
- [Perfect, actually. Rain outside, a book in here.|I've been reading all afternoon. The rain makes it better.|Rainy days are library days.] [I didn't even notice the time.|I'm halfway through a mystery.|Want to sit with me?]
- [Quiet. Rainy. Wonderful.|I found the best seat by the window.] [Exactly how I like it.|You can hear every drop.]
- [The rain chased everyone else away from my corner.|The library smells like rain and paper today.] [Lucky me.|I love it.]

@rule day.rain.outside.lover
on day
when kind=day wet=yes rainlover=yes
opens share,invite,tease
feel smile
- [Great! It's raining!|Best day this week. Look at it pour!|I went out in the rain at lunch. Don't tell.] [Everyone else is grumpy. I'm not.|I love days like this.|I'm still a little damp.]
- [Rainy days make me happy. I can't explain it.|I walked here the long way, in the rain.] [Weird, right?|On purpose.]
- [I wish it rained every day.|The rain's the only thing I like about today's schedule.] [Sorry, sunshine people.|Well, and you.]

@rule day.rain.energetic
on day
when kind=day wet=yes tone=energetic
opens tease,invite
feel pout
- [Terrible! It's raining!|Ugh, the rain ruined everything.|Practice got moved inside, so now we're all squashed in the gym.] [I wanted to run!|I'm going stir crazy.|Thanks, sky.]
- [I got splashed by a car this morning.|My umbrella flipped inside out.] [Full splash. Head to toe.|Everyone saw!]
- [I'm SO bored. Rain means no going outside.|Indoor lunch again.] [Entertain me!|Save me.]

@rule day.rain.gentle
on day
when kind=day wet=yes tone=gentle
opens share,comfort
feel smile
- [It's been a slow day... the rain makes everything soft.|Quiet. I like rainy days, a little.|I've been watching the rain from the window.] [I could fall asleep.|It's peaceful.|I hope it doesn't stop yet.]
- [My socks got wet this morning, but it's fine.|I lent my umbrella to someone and got rained on.] [Hehe.|It was worth it.]
- [Rainy days make me want to drink tea.|I'm a little sleepy. It's the rain.] [And talk.|Sorry.]

@rule day.rain.cool
on day
when kind=day wet=yes tone=cool
opens share,ask
- [Fine. Fewer people outside. Good.|It's raining. The halls are packed. Not ideal.|Quiet, until everyone crammed inside.] [Tolerable.|I'm managing.|I'd rather be home.]
- [I brought an umbrella. Some people didn't.|Wet shoes everywhere.] [They suffer.|Annoying.]
- [Rain suits my mood.|It's a good day to say nothing.] [Don't read into it.|Mostly.]

@rule day.rain.teasing
on day
when kind=day wet=yes tone=teasing
opens tease,invite
feel smile
- [Rainy and boring. Until now~|Wet. Dull. But you showed up.|Rain all day. I was hoping someone would rescue me.] [Lucky me.|Things are looking up.|Was it you?]
- [I got caught in the rain. See-through shirts are a hazard, you know.|My hair's a disaster today.] [Don't stare.|Say it's cute.]
- [Rainy days are made for cuddling indoors. Just saying.|The rain made everyone gloomy. Not me.] [Hint.|I'm too cute to be gloomy.]

@rule day.storm
on day
when kind=day weather=storm
opens comfort,share
feel worried
- [The storm's freaking me out.|Did you hear that thunder?|I jumped so high at the last one.] [I can't concentrate.|It's so loud.|Don't laugh.]
- [I hope the trains run home.|They might cancel club activities.] [I'm worried.|Probably.]
- [The lights flickered during class.|The wind broke someone's umbrella.] [Everyone screamed.|Poor thing.]

@rule day.rainlater
on day
when kind=day rainlater=yes
opens share,invite
- [Fine, but it looks like rain.|Okay so far. The sky's getting dark, though.|Good! I just hope the rain holds off.] [I forgot my umbrella.|I have practice later.|Fingers crossed.]
- [Everyone's talking about the rain later.|The forecast said heavy rain this afternoon.] [Should I leave early?|Great.]
- [I can smell it coming.|It's that heavy, quiet air before the rain.] [It's going to pour.|I kind of like it.]

@rule day.fight.place
on day
when kind=day fight=yes
opens comfort,ask
feel sad
- [Not great. {Fightwho} and I had a fight.|Honestly? Bad. Me and {fightwho} aren't talking.|I've been avoiding {fightwho} all day.] [It's stupid.|I don't want to make it bigger.|I'm tired.]
- [I keep replaying the fight with {fightwho}.|Everything reminds me of {fightwho} today.] [Ugh.|I hate it.]
- [Let's not talk about {fightwho}.|My day's... fine. Except {fightwho}.] [Distract me?|Ask me something else.]
